{
  "_comment": [
    "Every run in the project, in one versioned file. Runs are grouped by the",
    "collection they are scored on. MAP is only comparable *within* a group: a",
    "smaller collection has fewer wrong answers available and scores higher for",
    "free, so the report never puts two groups in one table.",
    "ftm2d_nodc_* zero the DC coefficient of the descriptor. It is ~97% of the energy and squeezes every distance into a narrow band; the pair is kept so the effect of removing it is a measured number rather than a claim.",
    "chroma_mean and chroma_mean_oti are a matched pair: the same average pitch-class profile, compared where it lies and compared at its best of twelve rotations. They differ in key invariance and nothing else, which is what makes a null key effect for the real methods mean something rather than being indistinguishable from an analysis too weak to detect anything."
  ],
